%T A397410 191,211,223,227,239,251,263,271,283,293,307,311,347,359,367,383,419,
%U A397410 431,443,463,467,479,487,491,503,523,547,563,571,587,599,631,643,647,659,683
%N A397410 Primes of the form p^2 + 2*q, where p and q are primes.
%C A397410 It appears that terms of the form 6*k - 1 occur significantly more frequently than terms of the form 6*k + 1. [This is because p^2 + 2*q == 1 (mod 6) implies p = 3 or q = 3. - _Jianing Song_, Aug 09 2026]
%e A397410 13 is a term because 13 = 3^2+2*2.
%e A397410 31 is a term because 31 = 3^2+2*11 = 5^2+2*3.
%o A397410 (PARI) isok(p) = isprime(p) && forprime(q=1, sqrtint(p), my(x=p-q^2); if (!(x%2) && isprime(x/2), return(1))); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Jul 28 2026
%Y A397410 Cf. A000040, A001248, A100484.
%K A397410 nonn
%O A397410 1,1
%A A397410 _Michael Shmoish_, Jul 28 2026
